From 4fcaadd644661fb219ad832e3a90c122189ab69d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Thu, 6 Aug 2026 19:02:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Implement wp_viewporter

mpv's wlshm video output hard-requires wp_viewporter ("Compositor
doesn't support the required wp_viewporter protocol!") and exits
without it; swayimg and GTK bind it opportunistically too.

A wp_viewport decouples a surface's size from its buffer's size:
the compositor samples a client-chosen source rectangle out of the
buffer (in buffer coordinates) and scales it to a client-chosen
destination size (in surface coordinates). The crop and scale
values are double-buffered surface state, so they live in
OwlSurfaceState next to the buffer and input region and follow the
same pending/current/copy-forward rules; the wp_viewport object
merely validates requests and writes into the pending state.

Committing now sizes the view as the spec dictates: destination
size if set, else the (integer) source rectangle size, else the
buffer size as before. Since input coordinates are surface-local,
hit testing, input regions and tracking rects keep working
unchanged on the scaled view.

Drawing gains an OwlBuffer -drawInRect:fromRect: primitive that
scales a buffer sub-rectangle into the view. The shm path crops
with CGImageCreateWithImageInRect, which only references the
original pixels and matches Wayland's top-left-origin buffer
coordinates (the GNUstep image-rep path flips the rect instead);
the IOSurface path selects the source rect via explicit rectangle
texture coordinates, which also fixes sampling for the case where
the view size differs from the buffer size (the old code reused
the vertex array as texture coordinates). Damage tracking with an
active viewport degrades to a full repaint: mapping surface-local
damage rects through a crop-and-scale is not worth the trouble,
and video players redraw every pixel each frame anyway.

The commit-time protocol errors are enforced per spec: bad_size
for a fractional source size with no destination to give it an
integer meaning, and out_of_buffer for a source rectangle that
sticks out of the attached buffer. set_source/set_destination
validate values eagerly (bad_value), and requests on a viewport
whose surface is gone raise no_surface via the destroy-listener
pattern.

Remember to re-run configure: this adds both a protocol XML and a
new .m file, which configure globs.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ATcm6iiwWVUU7Dmu6uXV4C
